OL,3,GNEWSARestoration completed on          
OL,4,A400-year-old gateway                   
OL,6,FA 17th-century gateway that once led   
OL,7,Ffrom the River Thames into one of      
OL,8,FLondon's grandest palaces has been     
OL,9,Frestored in its 400th anniversary year.
OL,11,FYork Watergate, in Victoria Embankment 
OL,12,FGardens, was built in 1626 as the      
OL,13,Fceremonial river entrance to York      
OL,14,FHouse, the home of George Villiers, the
OL,15,F1st Duke of Buckingham.                
OL,17,FIt now stands about 150m (490ft) from  
OL,18,Fthe water, having been left stranded   
OL,19,Finland when the Victoria Embankment was
OL,20,Fbuilt in the 19th century.             
